<div class="wrap about-prose">

  <section id="trainingpeaks">
    <h2>TrainingPeaks</h2>
    <p>I started by selling plans in their marketplace. Then I joined <strong>Coach Match</strong>: the limited directory TrainingPeaks refers athletes into when someone completes the questionnaire and has to be paired with a coach.</p>
    <p>A good share of those referrals in the region now reach me{% if site.coachMatchLeads %}, and I have spoken with more than {{ site.coachMatchLeads }} people who arrived that way{% endif %}. That's why I say I work in partnership with TrainingPeaks: not as a badge in a bio, but because the real flow of athletes runs through it. I'm also a <strong>Level&nbsp;2 Accredited Coach</strong> on the platform, and that accreditation is renewed every year.</p>
    <p>The {{ plans.byLanguage.en.length }} English plans in the catalogue live on that same platform. So does the 1:1 coaching.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Certifications</h2>
    <p class="about-papers"><span class="cred-inline">{% for item in cr.items %}{{ item.name }}{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}</span></p>
    <p>They are not the method. The method is the test, zones built from <em>your</em> numbers, the Monday check-in, and the re-test that confirms the progress was real rather than a feeling.</p>
    <p><a href="/en/training-zones-calculator/">Try the zone calculator</a> — it's public, it's the same one I use with my athletes, and it shows you concretely how I work before you talk to me.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="about-faq">
    <h2>Frequently asked</h2>
    <h3>Is Iván Koch on TrainingPeaks Coach Match?</h3>
    <p>Yes. TrainingPeaks refers endurance athletes to his roster through Coach Match, the platform's limited coach directory.</p>
    <h3>What accreditations does he hold?</h3>
    <p>TrainingPeaks Level 2 Accredited Coach, IRONMAN U Certified Coach, ESCI Certified Coach and Certified Stryd Coach.</p>
    <h3>What languages does he coach in?</h3>
    <p>Spanish, English and Portuguese.</p>
